  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1102 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe shortwave out west is progged to become more of a positively\ntilted open wave as it moves into the central/southern Plains \nThursday. Ahead of this wave, weak southerly low level flow looks \nto return Wednesday night into Thursday before an associated cold \nfront drops southeast into the CWA during the day Thursday. This \nperiod of return flow will open a brief window for moisture \nadvection back into the region, which will aid in rain chances\nreturning Thursday afternoon/evening. With limited moisture\nreturn, rainfall amounts should remain light. Latest model\nsolutions continue to highlight little instability ahead of the\nshortwave, and as such will continue to keep thunder potentials\nless than 10 percent. \n\nSlightly below seasonal average temperatures set in Friday in the\nwake of the departing shortwave and look to continue into  \nSaturday. Beyond Saturday, extended models differ with the track\nof another wave that could move through the Plains. For now will \nhold off on adding any PoPs into the forecast for the weekend,\nthough it is something to keep an eye on. If the wave can remain\nnorth and east of the CWA, then a return southerly winds and\nwarmer temperatures could develop for early next week.",
